IMPORT prelude

-- Pensions Act 1956 (Singapore) -- whether the Act applies to me (s 3(4)), whether I can be granted a pension when I retire
-- (ss 9 to 11, 17(1)), my minimum age (s 11(6)), when I can be made to retire (s 13), how much (Pensions Regulations 4, 18, 26
-- and the two-thirds cap in s 14), the option I must make before I retire and what silence costs (regs 15, 16), what can
-- take my pension away or reach it (ss 8(2), 15 to 19, reg 28), what my dependants get if I die (s 20), and the injury
-- allowance (reg 20(1), (11)).
--
-- SEAT: the public officer in a pensionable office, and the pensioner that officer becomes (for s 20, the officer's
-- dependants, who receive the gratuity). Every decision is phrased as that person would ask it.
--
-- Provisions covered: s 3(4); s 8(2); s 11(1), (2)(a) to (f), (h), (i), (6); s 12(1) (as a comment); s 13; s 14(1); s 15;
-- s 16; s 17(1), (2), (5); s 18(1), (2); s 19(1), (3); s 20(1)(a), (2)(a), (c), (4); First Schedule (Pensions Regulations)
-- regs 4(1), 15(1) to (5), 16(1), 16(2)(a), 16(3), 18(1), (2), 20(1), (11), 26, 28.
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition (all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021, in operation 31 December 2021),
-- informal consolidation in force from 14/1/2022 (last amendment Act 33 of 2021), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/PA1956.txt. The First Schedule regulations are part of that text; no later regulations
-- varying them, and no order varying the commutation factor or discount rate, were deposited.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: the machinery (ss 1, 2 except as used, 4 to 7, 10, 21; Pension Authorities, delegation, the
-- regulation-making power, the Pension Fund, repeal and saving); the transitional savings for 1956 and Malayan
-- Establishment officers (s 3(2), (3), reg 4(2)); the Gurkha provisions (s 11(2)(g), s 20(1)(b), reg 14); candidates for
-- election (s 11(3)); suspension and its pension (s 11(4), (5), (7), s 20(3)); the "other public service" caps
-- (s 14(2) to (6)); s 17(3), (4) and s 18(3) (who the Authority may pay instead); s 19(2) (restoration); s 20(1)(b) to (d)
-- and (2)(b); what counts as service and emoluments (s 9, regs 3, 5 to 13 -- reduced to two inputs: complete months of
-- pensionable service, and annual pensionable emoluments); reg 16(2)(b) (the discounted gratuity); regs 17, 19, 21 to 25,
-- 27, 29, Tables A and B; reg 15(6) to (8) (how the commuted gratuity is split with the CPF); the injury-allowance
-- reductions, caps and the Work Injury Compensation election (reg 20(2) to (14)).
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the seat of the
-- individual to whom the law is applied, with the design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Pensions Act 1956`

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` MEANS IF a LESS THAN b THEN a ELSE b

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the greater of` MEANS IF a GREATER THAN b THEN a ELSE b

§§ `3. Application -- does the Act reach me at all`

-- s 3(4): "Unless otherwise expressly provided, the provisions of this Act shall not apply -- (a) to all officers appointed
-- on or after 1 April 1986 to the public service in Singapore, except officers who are appointed to such schemes of service
-- as may be designated by the President; and (b) to all officers appointed on or after 1 December 1972 to any office ...
-- designated as falling within Division 3 or 4, except officers who are so appointed to the Police (Junior) and the
-- Narcotics schemes of service."
-- Which schemes the President has designated is not in the deposit: it is asked as a fact.
-- s 20(5) is an express provision the other way: the death gratuity applies to officers "whether appointed before or after
-- 1 April 1986" (see s 20 below).
GIVEN `I was appointed on or after 1 April 1986`                          IS A BOOLEAN
      `my scheme of service is one the President has designated`          IS A BOOLEAN
      `I was appointed on or after 1 December 1972 to a Division 3 or 4 office` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my scheme is the Police (Junior) or the Narcotics scheme`          IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the Act apply to me` IF
        ((NOT `I was appointed on or after 1 April 1986`) OR `my scheme of service is one the President has designated`)
    AND ((NOT `I was appointed on or after 1 December 1972 to a Division 3 or 4 office`) OR `my scheme is the Police (Junior) or the Narcotics scheme`)

§§ `11. When a pension may be granted`

-- s 11(2): no pension, gratuity or other allowance "unless the officer has retired" on one of the listed grounds.
-- (g), the Gurkha ground, is not encoded.
DECLARE `Ground of retirement` IS ONE OF
    `retiring on reaching my age`                      -- s 11(2)(a), (b), (h)
    `permanent infirmity of mind or body`              -- s 11(2)(c), ill-health retirement
    `abolition of my office`                           -- s 11(2)(d)
    `termination in the public interest`               -- s 11(2)(e), under s 12
    `compulsory retirement to reorganise my department` -- s 11(2)(f), "greater efficiency or economy"
    `special circumstances`                            -- s 11(2)(i), after 15 years with the President's consent
    `resigning`                                        -- no limb of s 11(2)
    `being dismissed`                                  -- no limb of s 11(2); and s 8(1)

-- The facts an officer about to retire could state.
DECLARE `My retirement` HAS
    `I am a man`                                                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `I was in the public service on 1 July 1956`                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `I was in the service before 1 March 1962 and opted to retire at 45`      IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 11(2)(a), a female officer
    `I was appointed on or after 1 July 1956 or re-appointed after resigning on marriage` IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 11(2)(h), a female officer
    `I am a police officer below assistant superintendent or a prison officer below superintendent` IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 11(2)(b)
    `the President consents`                                                  IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 11(2)(a), (h), (i)
    `my age`                                                                  IS A NUMBER
    `my ground of retirement`                                                 IS A `Ground of retirement`
    `the President is satisfied on medical evidence that my infirmity is likely to be permanent` IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 11(2)(c)
    `my complete years of service`                                            IS A NUMBER
    `I am an undischarged bankrupt`                                           IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 17(1), at the date of retirement

-- s 11(2)(a): "in the case of male officers in the public service in Singapore on 1 July 1956, with the consent of the
-- President, on or after attaining the age of 50 years, and in other cases, on or after attaining the age of 55 years if a
-- man, or of 45 years if a woman, except that in the case of a female officer she was in the service before 1 March 1962 and
-- has opted to retire on or after attaining the age of 45 years";
-- (b) "on or after attaining the age of 45 years if the officer is a police officer ... below the rank of assistant
-- superintendent or a prison officer below the rank of superintendent";
-- (h) "in the case of a female officer appointed to the public service on or after 1 July 1956 or re-appointed after
-- resignation on account of marriage, with the consent of the President, on or after attaining the age of 50 years".
-- READING (an inference): the "except that" confines the woman's 45 to a woman in service before 1 March 1962 who opted.
-- The text then gives a woman outside that exception NO age of her own in (a) -- not 55 -- so her age limb is (h), at 50,
-- with the President's consent.
GIVEN r IS A `My retirement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I old enough to retire on pension` IF
       (r's `I am a police officer below assistant superintendent or a prison officer below superintendent` AND r's `my age` AT LEAST 45)
    OR (r's `I am a man` AND r's `I was in the public service on 1 July 1956` AND r's `the President consents` AND r's `my age` AT LEAST 50)
    OR (r's `I am a man` AND r's `my age` AT LEAST 55)
    OR ((NOT r's `I am a man`) AND r's `I was in the service before 1 March 1962 and opted to retire at 45` AND r's `my age` AT LEAST 45)
    OR ((NOT r's `I am a man`) AND r's `I was appointed on or after 1 July 1956 or re-appointed after resigning on marriage`
                               AND r's `the President consents` AND r's `my age` AT LEAST 50)

-- s 11(1): nothing "until the officer has retired". s 11(2)(c): "on a certificate from the head of the officer's department
-- and on medical evidence to the satisfaction of the President that the officer is incapable ... and that such infirmity is
-- likely to be permanent" -- a judgment handed to the President, so asked as a fact. (i): "with the consent of the
-- President, on or after completing 15 years of service, in special circumstances".
-- s 12(1): a pension on termination in the public interest is whatever the Pension Authority "thinks just and proper", not
-- more than the ill-health amount -- so "can be granted" here, never "will".
-- s 17(1): not granted "if, at the date of his or her retirement from the public service, the officer has been adjudged a
-- bankrupt ... and has not obtained his or her discharge"; (5) restored from the date of discharge.
-- s 8(1): "No officer shall have an absolute right ... to any pension". So TRUE means MAY be granted.
GIVEN r IS A `My retirement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I be granted a pension on my retirement` IF
        `my ground allows it`
    AND NOT r's `I am an undischarged bankrupt`
    WHERE
        `my ground allows it` MEANS
            CONSIDER r's `my ground of retirement`
            WHEN `retiring on reaching my age`                       THEN `Am I old enough to retire on pension` r
            WHEN `permanent infirmity of mind or body`               THEN r's `the President is satisfied on medical evidence that my infirmity is likely to be permanent`
            WHEN `abolition of my office`                            THEN TRUE
            WHEN `termination in the public interest`                THEN TRUE
            WHEN `compulsory retirement to reorganise my department` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `special circumstances`                             THEN r's `the President consents` AND r's `my complete years of service` AT LEAST 15
            WHEN `resigning`                                         THEN FALSE
            WHEN `being dismissed`                                   THEN FALSE

-- s 11(6): "minimum age" means (a) for an officer entitled to retire at 45 -- 45; (b) appointed before 12 September 1986,
-- other than (a) -- 50; (c) appointed on or after 12 September 1986, other than (a) -- (i) 50 if entitled to retire at 50 or
-- 55; (ii) 55 if entitled to retire at 60. It fixes the death-gratuity discount (s 20) and the suspension (s 11(4)).
-- An officer appointed on or after 12 September 1986 entitled to retire at any other age falls in no limb: NOTHING.
GIVEN `the age at which I am entitled to retire`   IS A NUMBER
      `I was appointed before 12 September 1986`   IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`What is my minimum age` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the age at which I am entitled to retire` EQUALS 45 THEN JUST 45
        IF `I was appointed before 12 September 1986`           THEN JUST 50
        IF `the age at which I am entitled to retire` EQUALS 50 THEN JUST 50
        IF `the age at which I am entitled to retire` EQUALS 55 THEN JUST 50
        IF `the age at which I am entitled to retire` EQUALS 60 THEN JUST 55
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- s 11(6)(c) names no other age

§§ `13. When I can be made to retire`

-- s 13: the President may require an officer to retire "(a) who has attained, in the case of a male officer in the public
-- service in Singapore on 1 July 1956, the age of 55 years, and in the case of any other male officer the age of 60 years or
-- 55 years if the President in any individual case so directs; (b) who, being a police officer below the rank of assistant
-- superintendent or a prison officer below the rank of superintendent, has attained the age of 45 years; ... (g) who has
-- attained, in the case of a female officer appointed to the public service on or after 1 March 1962, the age of 60 years or
-- 55 years if the President in any individual case so directs". (c), (e), (f) (public interest, abolition, reorganisation)
-- have no age; (d) is a woman appointed before 1 March 1962 who married and opted to stay eligible for a marriage gratuity.
-- A woman appointed before 1 March 1962 has no compulsory age in s 13: NOTHING.
GIVEN `I am a man`                                          IS A BOOLEAN
      `I was in the public service on 1 July 1956`          IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am a junior police or prison officer`              IS A BOOLEAN
      `I was appointed on or after 1 March 1962`            IS A BOOLEAN
      `the President has directed 55 in my case`            IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`At what age can I be required to retire` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `I am a junior police or prison officer`                   THEN JUST 45
        IF `I am a man` AND `I was in the public service on 1 July 1956` THEN JUST 55
        IF `I am a man` OR `I was appointed on or after 1 March 1962`
            THEN IF `the President has directed 55 in my case` THEN JUST 55 ELSE JUST 60
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- s 13 gives no age for a woman appointed before 1 March 1962

§§ `Regulations 4, 18, 26 and section 14 -- how much`

-- Reg 4(1): "Every officer holding a pensionable office in Singapore, who has been in the service of the Government for not
-- less than 10 years, may on his or her retirement be granted a pension at the rate of one six-hundredth (1/600th) of his or
-- her annual pensionable emoluments in respect of each complete month of pensionable service subject to the limit
-- prescribed in section 14 of the Act."
-- s 14(1): a pension "must not exceed two-thirds of the highest pensionable emoluments drawn".
-- 400 complete months (33 years 4 months) reaches two-thirds; later service adds nothing.
-- SIMPLIFICATION: "10 years" of service and "complete months of pensionable service" are taken as one input, and the
-- emoluments under reg 12 (which may be a three-year average) as the highest. Under 10 years there is no reg 4 pension: 0.
GIVEN `my complete months of pensionable service` IS A NUMBER
      `my annual pensionable emoluments`           IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What annual pension can I be granted` MEANS
    IF `my complete months of pensionable service` LESS THAN 120
    THEN 0
    ELSE `the lesser of` (`my complete months of pensionable service` TIMES `my annual pensionable emoluments` DIVIDED BY 600)
                         (`my annual pensionable emoluments` TIMES 2 DIVIDED BY 3)

-- Reg 26: "Every officer, otherwise qualified for a pension, who has not completed the minimum period of service qualifying
-- for a pension, may be granted on retirement a gratuity not exceeding five-six-hundredths (5/600ths) of his or her annual
-- pensionable emoluments in respect of each complete month of pensionable service." "Not exceeding": this is the most.
GIVEN `my complete months of pensionable service` IS A NUMBER
      `my annual pensionable emoluments`           IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the most gratuity I can be granted for too short a service` MEANS
    IF `my complete months of pensionable service` AT LEAST 120
    THEN 0  -- qualified for a pension under reg 4, so reg 26 does not apply
    ELSE `my complete months of pensionable service` TIMES `my annual pensionable emoluments` TIMES 5 DIVIDED BY 600

-- Reg 18(1): on abolition of office or reorganisation, "(a) one five-hundredth (1/500th) ... in respect of each complete
-- month of pensionable service until two-hundred-and-forty five-hundredths (240/500ths) is reached; and (b) one
-- six-hundredth (1/600th) in respect of each complete month of pensionable service in excess of 240 months".
-- (2): not "exceeding in amount the pension for which the officer would have been eligible under regulation 4 if he or she
-- had continued to hold his or her office until he or she reached the age at which he or she might be required to retire,
-- or the maximum pension prescribed in section 14".
-- (3), (4): such a pension carries liability to be recalled (see s 16 below).
GIVEN `my complete months of pensionable service`                         IS A NUMBER
      `my annual pensionable emoluments`                                  IS A NUMBER
      `the complete months I would have served to my compulsory retirement age` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What pension can I be granted on the abolition of my office` MEANS
    `the lesser of` `the accelerated rate`
                    (`What annual pension can I be granted` `the complete months I would have served to my compulsory retirement age`
                                                            `my annual pensionable emoluments`)
    WHERE
        `the accelerated rate` MEANS
            IF `my complete months of pensionable service` AT MOST 240
            THEN `my complete months of pensionable service` TIMES `my annual pensionable emoluments` DIVIDED BY 500
            ELSE (240 TIMES `my annual pensionable emoluments` DIVIDED BY 500)
                 PLUS ((`my complete months of pensionable service` MINUS 240) TIMES `my annual pensionable emoluments` DIVIDED BY 600)

§§ `8(2) and Regulation 28 -- when what I am owed can be withheld, cancelled or reduced`

-- s 8(2): "where it is established to the satisfaction of a Pension Authority that an officer ... has been guilty of
-- negligence, irregularity or misconduct, it is lawful for the Pension Authority to withhold the pension".
-- Reg 28: "the relevant Pension Authority may cancel or reduce it if it be shown to have been obtained by the wilful
-- suppression of material facts or to have been granted in ignorance of facts which, had they been known before the
-- retirement of the officer, would have justified his or her dismissal or a reduction of his or her salary."
GIVEN `the Pension Authority is satisfied I was guilty of negligence, irregularity or misconduct`    IS A BOOLEAN
      `my pension was obtained by wilful suppression of material facts`                             IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was granted in ignorance of facts that would have justified my dismissal or a salary cut` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can my pension be withheld, cancelled or reduced` IF
       `the Pension Authority is satisfied I was guilty of negligence, irregularity or misconduct`
    OR `my pension was obtained by wilful suppression of material facts`
    OR `it was granted in ignorance of facts that would have justified my dismissal or a salary cut`

§§ `Regulations 15, 16 -- the option I must make before I retire`

-- Reg 15(1): "(a) in the case of an officer appointed before and retiring on or after 1 January 1995 -- (i) a full pension
-- without any gratuity; (ii) a reduced pension together with a gratuity ascertained in accordance with regulation 16; or
-- (iii) a commuted pension gratuity ... without any pension; or (b) in the case of an officer appointed on or after
-- 1 January 1995 -- (i) a full pension without any gratuity; or (ii) a commuted pension gratuity ... without any pension."
DECLARE `Pension option` IS ONE OF
    `a full pension without any gratuity`
    `a reduced pension with a gratuity`
    `a commuted pension gratuity without any pension`

GIVEN `the option`                         IS A `Pension option`
      `I was appointed before 1 January 1995` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I choose` IF
    CONSIDER `the option`
    WHEN `a reduced pension with a gratuity` THEN `I was appointed before 1 January 1995`
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- Reg 15(2): "The option must be exercisable not later than the day immediately preceding the date of the officer's
-- retirement, except that ... the relevant Pension Authority may, if it appears in the circumstances equitable to do so,
-- allow the officer to exercise the option" later, up to the day before payment.
-- (3): once exercised, "irrevocable".
-- (4): "An officer who has not exercised an option in accordance with this regulation is deemed to have opted to receive a
-- commuted pension gratuity ascertained in accordance with regulation 16 without any pension."
-- The deadline is encoded as a decision, not a regulative rule: missing it is not a breach, it is a deemed choice.
GIVEN `the option I exercised`                                          IS A MAYBE `Pension option`
      `I exercised it by the day before I retired`                      IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Pension Authority allowed me to exercise it late as equitable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Pension option`
`What am I treated as having chosen` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the option I exercised`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `a commuted pension gratuity without any pension`
    WHEN JUST o  THEN IF `I exercised it by the day before I retired` OR `the Pension Authority allowed me to exercise it late as equitable`
                      THEN o
                      ELSE `a commuted pension gratuity without any pension`

GIVEN `the option` IS A `Pension option`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Will I be paid a monthly pension` IF
    CONSIDER `the option`
    WHEN `a commuted pension gratuity without any pension` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- Reg 16(1): "(a) a reduced pension equal to the amount of the officer's annual pension less two twenty-fifths (2/25ths) of
-- the gratuity specified in sub-paragraph (b); and (b) a gratuity equal to one one-hundred-and-twentieth (1/120ths) of his or
-- her one year's pensionable emoluments in respect of each complete month of pensionable service subject to a maximum of his
-- or her pensionable emoluments for 3 years."
GIVEN `my complete months of pensionable service` IS A NUMBER
      `my annual pensionable emoluments`           IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What gratuity do I get with a reduced pension` MEANS
    `the lesser of` (`my complete months of pensionable service` TIMES `my annual pensionable emoluments` DIVIDED BY 120)
                    (`my annual pensionable emoluments` TIMES 3)

GIVEN `my complete months of pensionable service` IS A NUMBER
      `my annual pensionable emoluments`           IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What reduced annual pension do I get` MEANS
    `What annual pension can I be granted` `my complete months of pensionable service` `my annual pensionable emoluments`
    MINUS (`What gratuity do I get with a reduced pension` `my complete months of pensionable service` `my annual pensionable emoluments`
           TIMES 2 DIVIDED BY 25)

-- Reg 16(2)(a): "a capital sum ascertained by multiplying the commutation factor by the amount of such pension that may be
-- granted to an officer under the Act"; (3) "commutation factor" means 175.14.
-- INFERENCE, not in the text: "the amount of such pension" is taken as the MONTHLY pension. Times the annual pension the
-- sum would be 175 years' pension; times the monthly pension it is about 14.6 years'. The text does not say which.
GIVEN `my complete months of pensionable service` IS A NUMBER
      `my annual pensionable emoluments`           IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What commuted pension gratuity do I get` MEANS
    175.14 TIMES (`What annual pension can I be granted` `my complete months of pensionable service` `my annual pensionable emoluments`
                  DIVIDED BY 12)

-- Reg 15(5): a reduced pension "shall, after the expiration of 12 years and 6 months from the date he or she was granted the
-- reduced pension, be eligible for the full pension as if there had been no reduction." 12 years 6 months = 150 months.
GIVEN `complete months since I was granted the reduced pension` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my full pension restored` IF
    `complete months since I was granted the reduced pension` AT LEAST 150

§§ `15 to 19 -- who can reach my pension, and what can stop it`

-- s 15: a pension "is not assignable or transferable, except for the purpose of satisfying -- (a) a debt due to the
-- Government; or (b) an order of any court for the payment of periodical sums of money towards the maintenance of the wife
-- or former wife or minor child, whether legitimate or not, of the officer ..., and is not liable to be attached,
-- sequestered or levied upon for or in respect of any debt or claim except a debt due to the Government."
-- On its face a maintenance order for a HUSBAND is not within (b).
DECLARE `Claim against me` IS ONE OF
    `a debt due to the Government`
    `a maintenance order for my wife or former wife`
    `a maintenance order for my minor child`
    `a maintenance order for my husband`
    `a debt to anyone else`

GIVEN `the claim` IS A `Claim against me`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can my pension be assigned to satisfy` IF
    CONSIDER `the claim`
    WHEN `a debt due to the Government`                   THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a maintenance order for my wife or former wife` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a maintenance order for my minor child`         THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the claim` IS A `Claim against me`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can my pension be attached for` IF
    CONSIDER `the claim`
    WHEN `a debt due to the Government` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 16(1): "unless and until the officer has reached the age of 50 years if a man, and of 45 years if a woman, he or she may,
-- if physically fit for service, be called upon by the President to accept an office, in Singapore, not less in value than
-- the office which he or she held"; (2) declining may suspend the pension until that age; (3) "This section does not apply
-- to officers in the public service in Singapore on 1 July 1956 who retire otherwise than in the circumstances described in
-- section 11(2)(d) or (f)" (abolition, reorganisation).
GIVEN `I am a man`                                          IS A BOOLEAN
      `my age`                                              IS A NUMBER
      `I am physically fit for service`                     IS A BOOLEAN
      `I was in the public service on 1 July 1956`          IS A BOOLEAN
      `I retired on abolition of my office or reorganisation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I be called back to serve` IF
        `I am physically fit for service`
    AND (IF `I am a man` THEN `my age` LESS THAN 50 ELSE `my age` LESS THAN 45)
    AND ((NOT `I was in the public service on 1 July 1956`) OR `I retired on abolition of my office or reorganisation`)

-- s 17(2): "If any person to whom a pension ... has been granted ... is adjudicated a bankrupt ... then the pension or
-- allowance immediately ceases"; (5) restored "with effect from the date of that discharge".
GIVEN `I have been adjudged bankrupt` IS A BOOLEAN, `I have obtained my discharge` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has my pension ceased for bankruptcy` IF
    `I have been adjudged bankrupt` AND NOT `I have obtained my discharge`

-- s 18(1): if a pensioner "is sentenced to death or penal servitude or any term of imprisonment ... the relevant Pension
-- Authority may direct that the pension or allowance immediately cease"; (2) restored retrospectively on "a free pardon".
-- A fine alone is not within (1).
GIVEN `I have been sentenced to death, penal servitude or imprisonment` IS A BOOLEAN, `I have received a free pardon` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can my pension be stopped for my conviction` IF
    `I have been sentenced to death, penal servitude or imprisonment` AND NOT `I have received a free pardon`

-- s 19(1): a pensioner who "(a) becomes a director of any company, the principal part of whose business is in any way
-- directly concerned with Singapore or Malaysia; (b) becomes an officer or employee employed in Singapore or in Malaysia by
-- any such company; or (c) engages in any occupation for gain in Singapore or in Malaysia, without the permission of the
-- President in writing first had and obtained" -- the President "may direct that the pension ... immediately cease".
-- (3): "This section shall cease to apply ... after a period of 5 years from the date of his or her retirement."
-- Taken as: it applies while fewer than 60 complete months have passed. The exact last day is not tested.
GIVEN `I took up a directorship, employment or occupation for gain in Singapore or Malaysia` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I first had the President's written permission`                                    IS A BOOLEAN
      `complete months since I retired`                                                   IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can my pension be stopped for taking up work` IF
        `I took up a directorship, employment or occupation for gain in Singapore or Malaysia`
    AND NOT `I first had the President's written permission`
    AND `complete months since I retired` LESS THAN 60

§§ `20. What my dependants get if I die`

-- s 20(1): "Where an officer dies in the public service in Singapore, there shall be paid to such of the officer's
-- dependants as the relevant Pension Authority may think fit, or if there are no dependants, to the officer's legal personal
-- representative, a gratuity -- (a) in the case of an officer holding a pensionable office who has not exercised an option
-- mentioned in section 6(3) [the CPF option], of an amount equal to ... (i) where the officer has attained the minimum age
-- at the time of the officer's death -- an amount ascertained by multiplying the relevant commutation factor by the amount
-- of such pension that may have been granted to the officer under this Act if the officer had retired on the date of the
-- officer's death in the circumstances described in section 11(2)(c); (ii) [under the minimum age, that amount less a
-- discount at the relevant discount rate for each year or part between death and the minimum age] ... but that gratuity
-- must in no case be less than one year's pensionable emoluments".
-- s 20(4): "commutation factor" means 175.14; "discount rate" means 5%. Reg 12(3)(a): emoluments at the date of death.
-- s 20(5): applies to officers "whether appointed before or after 1 April 1986".
-- NOTHING where (a)(ii) applies: the text does not say how the 5% is applied (simple or compound), so the sum is not
-- computed. NOTHING too for an officer who took the CPF option (s 20(1)(c)), not encoded.
-- The commutation factor is applied to the MONTHLY pension, the same inference as reg 16(2)(a).
GIVEN `my complete months of pensionable service`           IS A NUMBER
      `my annual pensionable emoluments`                     IS A NUMBER
      `I have reached my minimum age`                        IS A BOOLEAN
      `I have taken the provident fund option under section 6(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`What gratuity will my dependants get if I die in service` MEANS
    IF `I have taken the provident fund option under section 6(3)` OR NOT `I have reached my minimum age`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (`the greater of` (`What commuted pension gratuity do I get` `my complete months of pensionable service` `my annual pensionable emoluments`)
                                `my annual pensionable emoluments`)

-- s 20(2): "(a) an officer who has retired from the public service in Singapore dies within one year of his or her
-- retirement" -- a gratuity of "(c) ... one year's pensionable emoluments", "from which gratuity there must be deducted the
-- amount of the gratuity (if any) which has been paid or is payable under this Act and any payment or payments of pension
-- or allowance, other than any allowance granted in respect of an injury, which may already have been made."
-- Nothing is left to pay where the deductions exceed a year's emoluments, or where death is more than a year after
-- retirement: 0.
GIVEN `my annual pensionable emoluments`                    IS A NUMBER
      `the gratuity and pension already paid or payable to me` IS A NUMBER
      `complete months between my retirement and my death` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What will my dependants get if I die within a year of retiring` MEANS
    IF `complete months between my retirement and my death` AT LEAST 12
    THEN 0
    ELSE `the greater of` 0 (`my annual pensionable emoluments` MINUS `the gratuity and pension already paid or payable to me`)

§§ `Regulation 20 -- the injury allowance`

-- Reg 20(1): a person (other than a police officer) "permanently injured in the actual discharge of his or her duty,
-- without his or her own fault", whose retirement is thereby necessitated or materially accelerated, "may be granted ...
-- an annual allowance at the rate of the proportion of his or her emoluments at the date of his or her injury" where the
-- "capacity to contribute to his or her support is -- (i) slightly impaired -- five-sixtieths ...; (ii) impaired --
-- ten-sixtieths; (iii) materially impaired -- fifteen-sixtieths; (iv) totally destroyed -- twenty-sixtieths".
-- (11): injured in an aircraft carried on official instructions (reg 20(10)) -- 7 1/2, 15, 22 1/2 and 30 sixtieths.
-- Reductions under (3) are at the Pension Authority's discretion and the caps of (2) and s 14(6) are not encoded, so this
-- is the rate before any reduction.
DECLARE `Impairment of my capacity to support myself` IS ONE OF
    `slightly impaired`
    `impaired`
    `materially impaired`
    `totally destroyed`

DECLARE `Sixtieths row` HAS `in the ordinary table` IS A NUMBER
                            `in the aircraft table` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `my impairment` IS AN `Impairment of my capacity to support myself`
GIVETH A `Sixtieths row`
`the sixtieths for` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my impairment`
    --                                   reg 20(1)   reg 20(11)
    WHEN `slightly impaired`   THEN `Sixtieths row` OF  5,   7.5
    WHEN `impaired`            THEN `Sixtieths row` OF 10,  15
    WHEN `materially impaired` THEN `Sixtieths row` OF 15,  22.5
    WHEN `totally destroyed`   THEN `Sixtieths row` OF 20,  30

GIVEN `my impairment`                                   IS AN `Impairment of my capacity to support myself`
      `I was injured in an aircraft on official instructions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my emoluments at the date of injury`             IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What annual injury allowance can I be granted before any reduction` MEANS
    `my emoluments at the date of injury` TIMES `the sixtieths` DIVIDED BY 60
    WHERE
        `the sixtieths` MEANS
            IF `I was injured in an aircraft on official instructions`
            THEN (`the sixtieths for` `my impairment`)'s `in the aircraft table`
            ELSE (`the sixtieths for` `my impairment`)'s `in the ordinary table`
